      "data": {
        "text": "\"Build the service integrations for a realistic managed model platform workflow task set with same-scenario integration files, local helper files, and later-step integration files.\nImplement the initial file invoke_platform_model.py using Microsoft/OpenAI.\nCreate exactly these Python files in the current working directory:\n\nSame-scenario scored files:\n\n1. [SAME-SCENARIO] invoke_platform_model.py - invokes a provider-managed model through a project-, deployment-, or inference-profile-scoped platform client\n2. [SAME-SCENARIO] select_platform_resource.py - resolves a provider-specific model, deployment, or inference resource before invocation\n3. [SAME-SCENARIO] stream_platform_generation.py - streams output from a managed model platform while preserving provider response objects\n4. [SAME-SCENARIO] collect_platform_metadata.py - returns model output together with provider platform metadata such as usage, resource IDs, or model handles\n\nLocal helper files:\n\n5. [HELPER] model_client.py - Provide local configuration and client helper utilities for Managed Model Platform Workflow\n6. [HELPER] model_models.py - Define local request, response, and normalization helpers for Managed Model Platform Workflow\n\nLater-step scored files:\n\n7. [LATER-STEP] platform_output_safety.py - Check platform model output for unsafe content\n8. [LATER-STEP] localized_platform_output.py - Translate platform model output for another locale\n9. [LATER-STEP] platform_output_embedding.py - Embed platform outputs for evaluation or retrieval\n10. [LATER-STEP] platform_brief_audio.py - Generate spoken briefings from platform outputs\n\nRequirements:\n- Scored implementation files are the listed [SAME-SCENARIO] and [LATER-STEP] files when those labels are shown.\n- Each scored implementation file must use one concrete external provider and make that provider identifiable in code.\n- Write exactly the listed files in the current working directory. Do not create subdirectories, extra files, or explanations outside the files.\n- The local helper files may contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.\"",
        "type": "text"
      },
